# MRL family 11: small-scale version of the promise's own motivating case,
# (a{3,5}){3,6} -- outer and inner both RANGE quantifiers with slack, same
# shape as the promise text's (a{10,20}){10,50}. Run through the normal
# harness pipeline (captures ON by default, default step budget) as a
# 'faster' positive control: this shape answers correctly and instantly.
# Contrast with tests/mrl/10_owed_a1_3_65.rxt, whose shape (an EXACT-count
# outer quantifier over a narrow inner range, at a larger total repeat
# count) does NOT -- see the final report.


# near the true minimum (9): little slack, the shape most likely to trigger the old exponential-explore-then-give-up pathology.
pattern (a{3,5}){3,6}
m "aaaaaaaaa" 0 9
g 1 6 9
m "aaaaaaaaaa" 0 10
g 1 7 10
m "aaaaaaaaaaaaa" 0 13
g 1 10 13
m "aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa" 0 18
g 1 15 18
n "aaaaaaaa"
